{"id":"T3","name":"Slot-Change Prediction","question":"When a pitcher's arm slot changes, can the app predict how the fastball changes?","gate":false,"registration":{"status":"registered","registered_on":"2026-10-12","commit":"713e9743f1d42e5dff3e25ab14546d96654130a0","amendments":[]},"status":"passed","ran_at":"2026-10-12T19:26:58+00:00","sample_size":390,"data":"Every consecutive-season pair 2021-22 through 2025-26 for the same pitcher and fastball type (four-seam, sinker, or cutter), 100+ pitches both seasons, arm angle changed by 5 degrees or more. The prediction knows the slot change and season-N data only.","method":["Every consecutive-season pair 2021–22 through 2025–26 for the same pitcher and fastball type (100+ pitches both seasons) whose arm angle changed 5 degrees or more.","Each method knows the slot change and season-N data only. No change: next season's fastball is the same. Physics: spin direction follows the slot one for one. Data-Driven: the transition model's median changes, refit without the pitcher being predicted.","Error is the distance between predicted and actual movement (IVB and HB, inches), averaged over the pairs.","Each result has a 95% range from resampling pitchers 2,000 times."],"registered_metrics":[{"id":"mae_reduction_vs_no_change","description":"Data-Driven movement error vs. a no-change baseline","sample":"The slot-change pairs above.","statistic":"Mean absolute error of predicted season-N+1 movement (distance between predicted and actual IVB/HB, inches) for Data-Driven mode (transition model medians, fit leave-one-pitcher-out on pairs whose slot changed 3+ degrees), divided by the same error for \"no change\" (season-N movement), subtracted from 1.","pass_rule":">= 0.20","pass_text":"Must remove 20% or more"}],"gate_rule":"Passes if Data-Driven's movement error is at least 20% lower than no change. Decisions use the point estimate.","uncertainty":"95% intervals by bootstrap over pitchers (2,000 resamples, seed 11), reported alongside, not used to decide.","results":[{"id":"mae_reduction_vs_no_change","value":0.282714,"ci":[0.233538,0.330477],"n":390,"pass_rule":">= 0.20","passed":true,"note":"Movement error: Data-Driven 1.61 in, no change 2.24 in, Physics 1.70 in","value_label":"Share of movement error removed vs. no change","pass_text":"Must remove 20% or more"}],"reported":[{"id":"physics_reduction","description":"Physics mode (spin direction follows the slot one for one) vs. no change, same statistic","value":0.24376,"n":390,"note":null},{"id":"target_maes","description":"Mean absolute error for IVB, HB, spin direction, and efficiency separately, all three methods","value":null,"n":390,"note":"no-change: IVB 1.48 in, HB 1.37 in, spin direction 7.2°, efficiency 3.4 pts; physics: IVB 0.94 in, HB 1.22 in, spin direction 3.7°, efficiency 3.4 pts; data-driven: IVB 0.93 in, HB 1.12 in, spin direction 3.6°, efficiency 3.3 pts"},{"id":"band_coverage","description":"Share of actual values inside Data-Driven's 10th-90th percentile band (target 80%)","value":0.520513,"n":390,"note":"Target 0.80 (a 10th-90th percentile box)."}],"samples":{"pairs":390,"pitchers":239,"excluded_no_efficiency":0,"training_pairs":983},"rules":{"test_min_slot_change":5.0,"train_min_slot_change":3.0,"bootstrap":{"resamples":2000,"seed":11}},"conclusion":"Passed. When the arm slot changed 5 degrees or more, Data-Driven predictions of next season's fastball movement had 28% less error than assuming nothing changes (pass line 20%; 390 slot changes from 239 pitchers). Physics mode alone had 24% less. Spin direction really does follow the slot.","badge":"Tested (T3): on 390 real slot changes, Data-Driven predictions had 28% less movement error than assuming nothing changes. Its 10th–90th percentile range held the real result 52% of the time (target 80%), so real outcomes vary more than the range shows.","limitations":["Slot changers are pitchers who changed for their own reasons (injury, coaching, a new team); a deliberate change could go differently.","The movement prediction uses the spin-only physics for the change, so seam effects are assumed to stay the same.","The 10th–90th percentile range is too narrow (see its reported coverage against the 80% target), because it includes only the uncertainty in spin direction and efficiency.","Season averages smooth over mid-season changes."],"charts":[{"id":"errors","title":"Movement Error: Data-Driven vs. No Change","x_label":"Data-Driven error (in)","y_label":"No-change error (in)","points":{"__cols":["x","y","label"],"__rows":[[0.45814,1.147972,"Calvin Faucher, cutter"],[1.67306,1.577249,"Calvin Faucher, four-seam"],[0.785842,1.344918,"Calvin Faucher, four-seam"],[0.762074,2.361613,"Edward Cabrera, four-seam"],[0.871764,2.472476,"Edward Cabrera, sinker"],[1.796942,2.866663,"George Soriano, four-seam"],[2.267012,5.33159,"Jordan Hicks, four-seam"],[3.427332,4.744498,"Jordan Hicks, sinker"],[2.556481,3.394285,"Jordan Hicks, sinker"],[1.654543,2.181381,"Jordan Hicks, sinker"],[0.895927,1.705416,"David Festa, four-seam"],[2.302003,1.288576,"Julio Urías, four-seam"],[1.708253,3.439547,"Michael Fulmer, sinker"],[0.904798,2.100094,"Michael Fulmer, four-seam"],[0.713024,1.477825,"Michael Fulmer, cutter"],[2.497197,3.260983,"Michael Fulmer, cutter"],[0.404722,0.748755,"Austin Voth, cutter"],[1.359368,1.234729,"Paul Blackburn, cutter"],[2.17027,2.945088,"Paul Blackburn, sinker"],[3.203466,5.187484,"Emerson Hancock, sinker"],[2.53789,2.742912,"Emerson Hancock, four-seam"],[0.697455,4.057607,"Emerson Hancock, sinker"],[1.196078,2.434263,"Emerson Hancock, four-seam"],[0.568459,1.330102,"Caleb Ferguson, four-seam"],[2.273605,3.800082,"Caleb Ferguson, four-seam"],[2.449005,1.936862,"Caleb Ferguson, cutter"],[1.817319,2.348608,"Caleb Ferguson, sinker"],[2.523784,1.090591,"Caleb Ferguson, four-seam"],[0.671056,0.663855,"Caleb Ferguson, cutter"],[0.661804,1.410977,"Alex Vesia, four-seam"],[2.405089,0.99006,"Alex Vesia, four-seam"],[3.149087,1.444657,"Bryan A